FINAL ANSWER:
## Bus factor: `lib/index.js`

**Reviewer: Troy Goode.** Douglas Christopher Wilson is a fallback, with a caveat below.

| Metric | Value |
|---|---|
| Commits (all time) | 62, from 25 authors |
| Troy Goode share of commits | 29 of 62 (47%) |
| Troy Goode share of current lines | 159 of 231 (69%) |
| File bus factor | 1 |
| Dependents | `package.json` (`"main"`), `test/error-response.js`, `test/example-app.js`, `test/issue-2.js` |

Line ownership comes from `git blame -w -C -C --ignore-rev 62628c0`. A plain blame credits 214 of 231 lines to "Fiona Formatter" because of the reformat commit `62628c0`, so I excluded it.

- **Troy Goode:** the only active owner. They made the last real change on 2026-04-10 (`lib: annotate handlers`) and were the only human committer in the last 12 months. They are the clear reviewer.
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson:** second by lines (22, about 10%). Their last commit was 2017-10-04, so they have been inactive for about 9 years. They can only be a secondary reviewer if you can reach them.
- **Everyone else:** each has 12 or fewer lines, and most last committed between 2013 and 2018. Only LuisEGR (2021) is more recent. None of them is a realistic reviewer.
- **Fiona Formatter:** a formatting-only commit, not a knowledge owner. Do not assign review to them.

**Risk: HIGH.** The file is the package entry point (`"main"`), and one person owns most of it. If you can't get Troy Goode, there is no second reviewer who knows the code. In that case, run the three dependent tests (`test/error-response.js`, `test/example-app.js`, `test/issue-2.js`) and treat them as the main safety check.

**Suggestions:**
1. Ask Troy Goode to review this change.
2. Use the PR as a chance to add a second reviewer who then learns the file.
3. Keep your edit separate from any formatting changes. The next blame on this file will show your commit, not the earlier authors, if the two are mixed.

I analyzed this one file inline and did not launch the `contributor-analyzer` agent. I did not compute a project-wide bus factor.

